// ============================================================================
//  Español Quest vocabulary  —  .minecraft/config/espanolquest/vocabulary.json
//  Latin American Spanish.
//
//  Each entry maps a Minecraft item ID to its Spanish word:
//    "word"    : the Spanish noun, without the article (required)
//    "article" : "el", "la", "los" or "las" — shows the gender (optional)
//    "accept"  : other words that also count as correct (optional)
//    "gender"  : "f" or "m", only when the article doesn't show it
//                (feminine words starting with a stressed "a" take "el": el agua, el hacha)
//  Saying the word with or without the article ("la manzana" / "manzana" /
//  "una manzana") always counts.
//
//  Keys:
//    "apple"          = minecraft:apple ("minecraft:" can be left out)
//    "*_log"          = every item whose ID ends in _log (oak_log, birch_log, ...)
//    "music_disc_*"   = every item whose ID starts with music_disc_
//    "create:wrench"  = items from other mods (write the full ID)
//  Exact IDs win over wildcards; the longest wildcard wins between wildcards.
//
//  "colors" are added AFTER the noun on colored items and agree with it:
//    red_wool -> la lana roja,  red_bed -> la cama roja,  red_carpet -> la alfombra roja
//    "m" = masculine form, "f" = feminine form (plural is added automatically),
//    "invariable": true = never changes (naranja, rosa...).
//
//  Your edits here are kept. Entries here override the mod's built-in list.
// ============================================================================
